# Line endings.
#
# The repo stores text as LF; Git checks it out with your platform's native endings (CRLF on
# Windows) and normalises back to LF on commit. Without this, files written from a Linux editor
# or CI show up as whole-file diffs and Git warns "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on every add —
# which is exactly what data/seeds/*.json and start.cmd have been doing.
#
# One-off after adding this file, to renormalise what's already committed:
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git commit -m "Normalise line endings via .gitattributes"
* text=auto

# Windows batch files must keep CRLF — some shells choke on LF-only .cmd/.bat.
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf

# Explicitly binary: never newline-convert, never diff as text.
# (.world saves are JSON, not binary — but they live in the gitignored saves/ anyway.)
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.exe  binary
